this week Eric loves tech asks are any  tablets hardware apps OS good for people  giving presentations conferences  classroom sales etc Eric it turns out  that tablets are very capable of giving  presentations and they're much easier to  bring into the conference room than a  big clunky laptop but the key to getting  things started comes in a word that no  tech journalist likes to sale out a  dongle for the iPad Apple sells a $50  digital AV Adapter that makes it very  easy to connect the tablet to a TV and  most projectors for Microsoft and  Android tablets there are many universal  micro USB to HDMI adapter it's actually  how I'm able to give this presentation  right now on the Galaxy Note pro you can  also use wireless display features like  Apple's AirPlay or DLNA and some Windows  tablets have some form of video out  right on the tablet software is easy  this week I reviewed tablets with all  the major platforms Android iOS and  Windows and all of them have  alternatives to PowerPoint  Apple has keynote google has  presentations in its drive suite and  Windows has authentic PowerPoint just be  aware if you're buying a tablet with the  full version of Windows 8 you have to  buy the full version of Office to get  PowerPoint presenting on tablets is as  easy as swiping on the screen but if you  want to walk around the room you can get  a Bluetooth remote control there's this  one called the digit 2 our last tip just  don't make those presentations too  boring and we want to hear more of your  questions send them to us on Twitter or  Facebook with the hashtag ask WS JD now  back to my very important presentation
 

